Basic Rules of Penetration Testing
Understood that penetration testing must always be performed with proper authorization and legal permission.
Learned the importance of defining scope and objectives before starting a test.
Studied the need to follow a structured methodology (recon → scanning → exploitation → reporting).
Recognized the responsibility to avoid damaging systems or data during testing.
Learned that findings must be documented clearly with evidence and remediation suggestions.
Understood ethical responsibilities such as confidentiality and responsible disclosure.
Learned that penetration testing focuses on identifying vulnerabilities, not causing disruption.
